  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Drop pass and chase – 1v1",
  "description": "Use two cones to mark an area in front of goal, roughly an extension of the penalty area. Two queues, A and B, at the centre line. Goalkeeper in goal.\n\nA skates forward with the ball and B follows slightly behind. A drops the ball back to B and in that moment becomes the defender. B takes the ball into the marked area and tries to score while A turns, chases and tries to win it back. Play goes on until a goal, a save or the ball leaves the area.\n\nSwap queues after each go; B brings the ball back. Progression: A may only start chasing once B has received, or a second defender starts from the centre line. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Leave the ball so it sits still or rolls gently into your team-mate's path."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "B receives at speed and attacks at once – give the defender no time to recover."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "A: turn quickly, get level and steer B towards the board rather than diving in."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "This is a game drill – full speed and a real contest."
    }
  ],
